From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026
Subject: [PATCH] rsa-sign: handle OpenSSL provider store errors

Follow-up to 0005 (Add support for OpenSSL Provider API). The imported
patch has three defects in the provider branch of rsa_pem_get_priv_key():

- OSSL_STORE_load() returning NULL only drains the OpenSSL error queue
  and retries, so a persistent store error spins and a truncated key
  floods the log with repeated error dumps. Check OSSL_STORE_error()
  and fail out of the loop.
- A store that holds no private key leaves private_key NULL and the
  function returns 0, so the caller proceeds until EVP_PKEY_CTX_new()
  fails with an unrelated message. Return -EPROTO when no key was read.
- The FILE opened at the top of the function is closed only on the PEM
  path; the provider path reads the file again through OSSL_STORE_open()
  and leaks it. Close it before opening the store.

Also correct the source file name printed by drain_openssl_errors().

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>

---
 lib/rsa/rsa-sign.c | 18 +++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lib/rsa/rsa-sign.c b/lib/rsa/rsa-sign.c
--- a/lib/rsa/rsa-sign.c
+++ b/lib/rsa/rsa-sign.c
@@ -50,7 +50,7 @@ static void drain_openssl_errors(int l, int silent)
 	if (ERR_peek_error() == 0)
 		return;
 	if (!silent)
-		fprintf(stderr, "At main.c:%d:\n", l);
+		fprintf(stderr, "At rsa-sign.c:%d:\n", l);
 
 	while ((e = ERR_peek_error_line(&file, &line))) {
 		ERR_error_string(e, buf);
@@ -255,6 +255,9 @@ static int rsa_pem_get_priv_key(const char *keydir, const char *name,
 	EVP_PKEY *private_key = NULL;
 	OSSL_STORE_CTX *store;
 
+	/* The store reads the file on its own. */
+	fclose(f);
+
 	if (!OSSL_PROVIDER_try_load(NULL, "default", true))
 		ERR(1, "OSSL_PROVIDER_try_load(default)");
 	/* pkcs11 provider is optional; only needed for pkcs11: URIs */
@@ -268,7 +271,13 @@ static int rsa_pem_get_priv_key(const char *keydir, const char *name,
 		OSSL_STORE_INFO *info = OSSL_STORE_load(store);
 
 		if (!info) {
-			drain_openssl_errors(__LINE__, 0);
+			if (OSSL_STORE_error(store)) {
+				OSSL_STORE_close(store);
+				fprintf(stderr, "Failure reading private key: '%s'\n",
+					path);
+				ERR_print_errors_fp(stderr);
+				return -EPROTO;
+			}
 			continue;
 		}
 		if (OSSL_STORE_INFO_get_type(info) == OSSL_STORE_INFO_PKEY) {
@@ -281,6 +290,11 @@ static int rsa_pem_get_priv_key(const char *keydir, const char *name,
 	}
 	OSSL_STORE_close(store);
 
+	if (!private_key) {
+		fprintf(stderr, "No private key found in '%s'\n", path);
+		return -EPROTO;
+	}
+
 	*evpp = private_key;
 #else
 	if (!PEM_read_PrivateKey(f, evpp, NULL, path)) {
